    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 3,
        "sourceEnd": 51,
        "text": "Hi, Lin. You look busy. What are you working on?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "a45fdbe1e9256f58f116a7715dd047a6e3d2a637c39a4653cb5e7d8977d1a8c9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 55,
        "sourceEnd": 166,
        "text": "Oh, hi, Mark. I’m looking at the results of our college survey. We asked 200 students about their study habits.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "58754fa8a76e90e7b17621f06b864fd4b42573f1d48dcdf9241824a19c47bc09",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 170,
        "sourceEnd": 223,
        "text": "Two hundred? That’s a good number. What did you find?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "c34c34da4989a4b2c3d215cecc1209902b029540c8ed966939b8e78586b8d860",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 227,
        "sourceEnd": 387,
        "text": "Well, the biggest group—about 45 percent—said they study in the library. Another 30 percent study at home. The rest, 25 percent, study in cafes or other places.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "3201a80eec6b41d6cfb4e8acc44c8685e85030c27c7ef3c002f64aa5190fbf9e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 391,
        "sourceEnd": 467,
        "text": "So the library is the most popular. What about the time they spend studying?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "0a36f11f42ecc17867de123db3f126992dd1a1bb15c37a3e8362ccf27c4dc1f1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 471,
        "sourceEnd": 595,
        "text": "Last year, students studied about 10 hours a week on average. This year, it’s 12 hours. So there was an increase of 2 hours.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "de1b09c3d9ba3046142b8a1070c4704a06ab6ba1b03e596943bf0e49ebdd0c53",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 599,
        "sourceEnd": 670,
        "text": "That’s interesting. Did you compare first-year and final-year students?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "d5d7d632fcfd1654572959afdbc2de6c79805c1f17d5b4da5e8a04c4ac8dc1b0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 674,
        "sourceEnd": 834,
        "text": "Yes. First-year students study about 9 hours a week, but final-year students study 15 hours. So final-year students study 6 hours more than first-year students.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "27ec7564498285ffb12a07de22325cfeb6c9a6c9d19e5710d77c194f7b014a92",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 838,
        "sourceEnd": 922,
        "text": "That’s a big difference. What about the number of students who use online materials?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "640b5699ccef57d199070f84cd232cef542b7951eb18988a6239a72f496ba7ef",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 926,
        "sourceEnd": 1035,
        "text": "Two years ago, only 20 percent used online materials regularly. Now, it’s 60 percent. There was a sharp rise.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "28f9c9f8bd2866bfb4a83b16002eb96bfb21177f1370b2ad7281ebb0f7533d49",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1039,
        "sourceEnd": 1102,
        "text": "Wow, that’s three times more. Did you ask about part-time jobs?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "51aee10204823c9b15b91fc9be80a97d4d20a7879df35a3ded910d49313f5ea3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1106,
        "sourceEnd": 1243,
        "text": "Yes. In the survey, 40 percent of students have a part-time job. But last year, it was 50 percent. So there was a decrease of 10 percent.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "2e8b32ff9871d871d86234984c5f26f9975c917e687629232a160fb4c7fccddc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1247,
        "sourceEnd": 1272,
        "text": "Why do you think that is?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "f3755db8ffe4b9341dae31e1eeac463c6bab32161ad4afe58d3fc0a5cf392e22",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1276,
        "sourceEnd": 1345,
        "text": "Maybe because more students study longer hours now. But I’m not sure.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "55c516261fc615c23cebb5b847390f3878f3eaa988f6a06462fbd2f143ad1b41",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1349,
        "sourceEnd": 1379,
        "text": "Did you find any other trends?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "aa2446fa616806184de4cc30aad16ec5168bdc80cb4b92040b7b8635a04796f0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1383,
        "sourceEnd": 1534,
        "text": "Well, the number of students who study in groups increased from 15 percent to 25 percent. And individual study decreased from 70 percent to 55 percent.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "ce76de172d80dd4ef02ae78b44e0c0a793fd97d902b1af6d93e0bea4a2067451",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1538,
        "sourceEnd": 1627,
        "text": "So group study is becoming more popular. What about the library? Was it busier this year?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "e19c67efd3ad8d543af78bbbd6662e0a34c958548c28f613a64a673c89445a8b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1631,
        "sourceEnd": 1785,
        "text": "Yes, the library reported 500 more visits per week this year compared to last year. Last year there were 2,000 visits per week; this year there are 2,500.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "e39f534b56ce78126842f44cb98287fcd93137c934a92a499518dfafb6f1c591",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1789,
        "sourceEnd": 1872,
        "text": "That’s a 25 percent increase in visits. Good work, Lin. This data is really useful.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "de8b78203c6b5887a76b8620676a91193528d0b4285c3073412b01309849a79c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1876,
        "sourceEnd": 1930,
        "text": "Thanks, Mark. I’m presenting it to the class tomorrow.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "963967672adb78a0beed56a1744de2140001d49f78baeb6ff37f77ab88d3d76c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
